title: 'sp-arithmetic: reject nonzero targets for empty normalization input'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Normalizing an empty input to a nonzero sum previously returned an empty vector, even though
    the result could not have the requested sum. It now returns an error. An empty input with a
    zero target still returns an empty vector. The assignment normalization documentation in
    `sp-npos-elections` now describes the corresponding error case for empty distributions.
    Phragmen elections skip normalization for voters without elected edges, so voters who only
    approved losing candidates and elections with no seats still succeed.
    The benchmarking solver omits voters with no selected winner from its assignments, so their
    positive stake does not reach downstream normalization. The multi-phase miner drops
    assignments emptied by backer-limit trimming before normalization.
crates:
- name: sp-arithmetic
  bump: patch
- name: sp-npos-elections
  bump: patch
- name: frame-election-provider-support
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-election-provider-multi-phase
  bump: patch
